        "The thalamus is a relay station for sensory information. It relays information from the sensory organs to the cerebral cortex.",
        "Propranolol is a beta 1 adrenoceptor antagonist.  Beta 1 adrenoceptors are found in the heart and the juxtaglomerular cells of the kidney.  Beta 1 adrenoceptor agonists (e.g. dobutamine) are used to treat heart failure and beta 1 adrenoceptor antagonists (e.g. propranolol) are used to treat angina, hypertension and heart palpitations.  M2 muscarinic agonists (e.g. bethanechol) are used to treat urinary retention and M2 muscarinic antagonists (e.g. atropine) are used to treat bradycardia.  Alpha 1 adrenoceptor agonists (e.g. phenylephrine) are used to treat hypotension.",
        "Vitamin A is required for the formation of rhodopsin, a light-sensitive protein found in the retina. Night blindness is a symptom of vitamin A deficiency. Vitamin A and vitamin E are both fat soluble vitamins. They are absorbed in the small intestine via micelles. Excess vitamin E can inhibit the absorption of vitamin A.",
